Turen JSON Query wraps the jaq library crates — jaq-core 3.1.1,
jaq-json 2.0.3, and jaq-std 3.0.3 — a pure-Rust jq implementation by
Michael Färber and contributors, distributed under the MIT License.
Upstream: https://github.com/01mf02/jaq

The upstream CLI, module loading, filesystem access, environment access,
and clock access are not exposed; this package exposes only the bounded
wasm-bindgen operations documented in README.md.

Transitive Rust dependencies used by the compiled module are licensed under
permissive terms (MIT, Apache-2.0, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, BSL-1.0, or the
Unlicense; self_cell is elected under Apache-2.0 from its
Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-only dual license). The compiled module also uses
Rust standard-library components distributed under Apache-2.0 or MIT.
See Cargo.lock for the complete pinned dependency closure.
